---
code: lend-map-unknown-dimension
when-fires: an unknown lend_map dimension token appears on a `__lend_map` line. oracle/wrapper.rs walk_lend_body. `{expected}` = the known-dimension list.
why: 273 §8: the line mints no lend and the dimension it meant to answer walls. NOTE plain-language pass owed: ⊤/top wording (law-plain-language-surfaces, 24H ack-4).
---
-- oracle.sh --
# dorc-lang/v0.2
runas__lend_map() {
   printf '%s\n' "$1" : lends frobnicate
}

-- replay --
$ dorc lint oracle.sh --no-tools
dorc lint findings (advisory; the machine format `--format=jsonl` is the stable surface):

oracle.sh:
  warning[lend-map-unknown-dimension]: `frobnicate` is not a context dimension
  Dorc knows; a `__lend_map` line names one of user, fs-view, netns, so this
  line lends nothing and the dimension it meant to answer stays walled.
